    "summary": "Added Router (src/daemon/threads/router.ts), the IpcServer's forward on the main thread. It classifies each request with classOf. A routed class goes as a RequestEnvelope to the worker registered for it, and that worker's replies and frames come back over the channel attached for it (attach/detach). Other requests run through the local directDispatch, as before. A request whose class has no registered worker is held until one registers and is attached (targetsChanged), for at most holdMs (30 s by default); after that it is answered \"the daemon's <class> thread is not available\". On socket close, a stream gets a CancelEnvelope on its worker; a unary request is left to finish and its late reply is dropped. detach() returns a dead worker's in-flight requests, for the supervisor (t14) to fail. With daemon.threads.enabled, main() now uses the router as the server's forward with no class routed yet: each class is routed once its worker exists (admin in t10, indexing in t11). The server's registry hook publishes clients to the board before each request is forwarded.",
